> On Wednesday, August 26, 2015 11:01:14 selpa'i wrote:
>> I don't think {simbi'o} means what you want. {simbi'o} means "x1
>> (plural) become mutual in property x2".
>
> What's the difference between {simbi'o} and {bixsi'u}?

simbi'o
= x1 binxo lo ka ce'u simxu x2
= "x1 become mutual in x2"

E.g. {mi'a simbi'o lo ka prami} "We fell in love (with each other)."

bixsi'u
= x1 simxu lo ka ce'u binxo ce'u
= "x1 become each other"

(This one requires a concrete binxo2 to be useful)

E.g. {mi'a bixsi'u} "We have turned into each other."

